WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.168
Harry: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.437
we wanted to find out all the
differences between Ikea food

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.872
in the US and the UK.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.107
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.244
Quick note: It turns
out Ikea does not offer

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.213
a takeout option, but
fortunately they do sell

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.581
lots of Tupperware containers.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.782
So in case you're wondering why the food

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.850
looks a little bit sad,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.685
it's because we had to
improvise. On with the video.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.821
Let's start portion sizes
with Ikea's claim to fame

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.691
when it comes to food,
the Swedish meatballs.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.061
In the US, Ikea's restaurant
offer only one portion size

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.696
for meatballs, eight pieces,

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.832
but after that you can get
them in increments of four.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:37.337
For instance, 12 meatballs.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.039
In the UK, Ikea's iconic meatballs

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.809
come in two portion sizes, eight or 12.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.911
You can also add four extra
meatballs to any order

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.247
for an extra £1.75, and there's seemingly

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.282
no limit to how many
times you can do this.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.518
In the UK, the meatballs come
with either mashed potatoes

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:54.454
or chips on the side, as
well as some garden peas,

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.557
lingonberry jam, and of
course their famous gravy.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.793
And of course the meatball
options all come with a side

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.229
of mashed potatoes and
peas. Get a load of that.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.898
Also a little bit of cranberry sauce.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.699
We're going to weigh eight
meatballs in both countries

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.201
to see whose meatballs are bigger.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.770
One, two,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.173
three, four,

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.108
five, six,

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.210
seven, and eight.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.347
Let's also try and weigh our mash.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.583
Now, I do feel like the stats
might be skewed slightly

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.418
because there's some
peas embedded in this.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.487
I will try and free it where I can.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.627
We got way more mash than
the UK, like almost double!

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.831
They're feeding us at our Ikeas.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.733
Vegans and vegetarians,
rejoice. Ikea also offers

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.870
vegetarian-vegan versions
of its meatballs right here.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.240
We're doing a blind taste
test, plant versus meat.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.910
That's definitely plant-based.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.744
What's the next one?

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.979
Peter: No.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:53.913
Oh, was that wrong?

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.448
Wait, OK, give me another one.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.517
OK, this is the other one?

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.088
Yeah, that's meat. Not even close.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.290
Not even close. Thank you, Peter.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.792
Neither were bad.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.194
And if I was a vegetarian or vegan,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.997
I would be perfectly happy
with those plant balls.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:15.468
Tasted perfectly fine, but
the difference is noticeable.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.303
We share a couple of
dessert options with the US,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.638
notably the Daim cake.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.874
Over here, we call that
the caramel almond cake.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.041
Let's weigh a slice.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.046
Another dessert option
we share with the UK

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.381
is the soft-serve ice cream,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.717
which you get in vanilla or strawberry.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.253
OK, first of all, the
gentleman who worked there

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.355
was adamant that's actually frozen yogurt.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.422
I don't know if that's true or not.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.192
Regardless, they didn't have to-go cups

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.495
like Harry was able to get,
so all they would give us

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:45.798
is the small cup where
it's kind of poking out

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.799
like it's ready to eat.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.669
It is 97 degrees in Los Angeles today.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.772
There was absolutely no way
that was making it from Ikea

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.908
to the car, let alone the studio.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:58.178
So here's footage of me enjoying
it in the lobby of Ikea.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.213
So, I'm sorry I didn't bring the scale.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.447
I don't know how much it weighs.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.416
We have soft-serve ice
cream in the UK too,

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.752
either as vanilla or vanilla
with chocolate sauce.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:08.221
Impressively, they've
given us exactly 100 grams

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.355
of soft-serve ice cream.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.057
Ikea is also known for its hot dogs.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.226
In the UK you can get
either a classic hot dog

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.128
or a veggie hot dog from the bistro stand.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:16.829
We're going to measure and
weigh the classic hot dog

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.765
to compare with the US.

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.000
The hot dog in the UK
is 7 inches in length,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.435
and with the toppings
of pickles and onions,

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.370
it weighs 114 grams.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.072
Hot dog.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.709
Our hot dog is 5 ¼ inches long,

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:33.146
and our hot dog weighs 75 grams.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.052
Here are all the menu items from a UK Ikea

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.486
that you won't find in the US.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.122
Here's all the food
you'll find in a US Ikea

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.824
you won't find in the UK.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:48.061
Starting out down here, hot entrées.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.264
This single piece of chicken
is the Havana chicken.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.167
Now, it doesn't come alone.
It comes with plantains,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.469
rice, and beans, which we
will see in a little bit.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.638
But just isolated, the chicken,

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.506
has been sitting for a minute, sorry.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.942
Havana chicken. I wonder
what makes it so Havana.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.446
Yeah, I'm definitely
getting some spices in here.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:10.183
Very flavorful, not just, like,
a standard piece of chicken.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.217
It's actually really good.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.119
We'll start down this end
with some main courses.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.989
We have two different
nonmeat-meatball options in the UK.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.490
Firstly, we have the veggie balls.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.758
These are meatballs which are formed

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:19.926
of ground-up vegetables,

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.528
and they're also served with
a vegetable couscous as well.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.197
But for vegetarians who
prefer something a bit more

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.899
reminiscent of meat, they
also have plant balls.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:27.900
Now, I'm kind of intrigued by these

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.935
because they look really good.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:32.305
These are a fake-meat version
of Ikea's classic meatballs.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.007
Now, compared to a classic meatball,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.942
they're actually almost
more visually appealing,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.878
I would say. They're a nice,
dark, golden brown color.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.080
They look like they've been
cooked in a similar way,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.715
maybe even kind of fried

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:45.585
or cooked for longer than
you would expect from these.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:48.087
Let's do a very quick taste
test. Classic meatball.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.225
We all know and love it.
These things are delicious.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.826
And then one of the plant balls.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:57.930
I will say the plant-based
one doesn't have that

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.433
distinct Ikea meatball taste to it.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.135
That said, still pretty tasty.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.871
I think texture-wise,
it's almost identical

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:05.905
to the classic meatball.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.474
You can also get a salmon
filet with pea pesto,

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.311
vegetable medallions, and a corn medley,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.112
which you can see right here.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.148
I mean, salmon's OK, I guess.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:18.651
OK. This isn't, it's
been sitting for a while.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.621
If you like salmon, sure.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.623
I don't know, you go to
Ikea, you get salmon?

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:24.957
Pea pesto's interesting though.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.627
Still in the mood for fish

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.729
before you go furniture shopping?

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.899
You can also get the garlic
lemon cod with, of course,

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.500
mashed potatoes and peas.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.469
Actually, that's a pretty
good piece of fish.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.237
Yeah, I actually really like that.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.006
OK, I stand corrected.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:44.444
I was dissing the fish.
It's actually pretty good.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:47.880
We have a British classic dish,
and that's fish and chips.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.616
Now, the fish they serve at
Ikea in the UK is pollack.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:54.354
It comes with chips, peas,
and some tartar sauce.

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.189
Now, unlike fish and
chips that you might find

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.890
from a classic chippy in the UK,

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.459
they've actually breaded their fish

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.260
rather than battered and then fried it.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.363
I generally prefer the
battered fish texture.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.031
I like the kind of crispy
crunch on the outside

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.132
that you get from batter.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.369
I'm going to have a little try of this.

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.437
It's very weird tasting
things on "Food Wars"

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.906
using a knife and fork. I don't like it.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:17.009
I respect that they have
attempted to localize their menu

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.678
to the UK market.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:22.615
But maybe put a bit more
thought into your R&amp;D there.

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.250
If you want to see what proper
fish and chips looks like,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.651
go and check out our "Food Tours"

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.620
best fish and chips in London video.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:31.190
Next up we have another fish
option. It's a salmon filet.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.792
Charlie: Fillet.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.460
Leon: Come on.

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:38.631
Next up we have another fish
option. It's a salmon fillet.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:41.401
In the UK, we generally
lean more towards "fillet"

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:44.003
as the wording, and also we
spell it slightly differently.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:46.406
Often we spell it with two L's,
whereas I believe in the US

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.807
it tends to be spelled with one.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.809
I think you can get a
salmon fillet in the US.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:50.943
However, like we say,

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.211
we pronounce ours slightly differently,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:55.381
and also in the UK ours comes
with the veggie couscous.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.250
Chicken tenders. I mean, come on.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.687
Comes with fries and broccoli.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:05.925
Hm, wait, these tenders
are actually very good.

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:08.728
Like, the breading,
they're really breaded.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.263
Decent fries. Hearty.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.799
Ikea also has a few things on the menu

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:15.034
that were not available
at the one we went to.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.437
A chicken thigh with
garlic chipotle sauce,

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:19.305
broccoli, and rice. Sounds
actually pretty good.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:22.074
Lingonberry barbecue
ribs with mac 'n' cheese.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.243
Ah! I was so mad they didn't have those.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.878
And a plant-based burger with fries,

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:27.914
also not available at
time of filming this.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:31.851
Now, lingonberries are majorly
popular in Swedish cuisine,

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.386
and you're going to see
them pop up a few more times

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.253
in the Ikea menu.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:36.722
Next up is penne pasta with tomato sauce.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.991
Penne, of course, refers
to the shape of pasta

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:40.860
that they use here in Ikea.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.029
[Charlie laughing]

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:43.896
Charlie's loved that.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.608
I think penne is maybe my
least favorite pasta shape.

00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:58.411
I do not respect penne.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:07:59.545
Moving swiftly on from the penne,

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.447
we have a chicken katsu curry.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.249
I think this is a relatively new addition

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:04.450
to the UK Ikea menu.

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:07.286
So, katsu refers to the
chicken katsu fillet,

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:09.355
which is a breaded and
fried piece of chicken,

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.724
and then it's served with
rice and katsu sauce.

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:13.292
I've not tried this before.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.962
That looks like one just massive
piece of chicken, you know?

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:19.232
Science.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:21.968
Other than a couple of
slightly disconcerting

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:24.203
dark patches inside the chicken breast,

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.972
it's actually not bad. I
think because of the size

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:28.040
of the breast it's dried out quite a lot,

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.042
but the katsu sauce is really nice.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.110
I like it with the rice.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.745
I think particularly
if we'd eaten this hot,

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:33.813
this actually would be pretty good.

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.448
Next up on the UK menu you can find

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:38.384
a potato and cauliflower rogan josh curry.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:40.620
A rogan josh is a curry
that you'll find on the menu

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.021
of a lot of UK curry houses.

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:44.090
It's not super spicy,
generally quite mild.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.425
I'd say traditionally you
would see this made with lamb,

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:47.994
but they've made a
vegetarian version here,

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:49.495
obviously with potato and cauliflower

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.730
as the main bulk of it.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.999
The rogan josh from Ikea
is served with rice,

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:55.101
and then you can also
get some side options

00:08:55.101 --> 00:08:58.037
which are designed to go with
it, including some pakoras,

00:08:58.037 --> 00:09:00.172
samosas, and a garlic naan.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.708
Obviously the UK has a large
British Indian population,

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.076
so I do think this is another attempt to

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:05.378
kind of localize the menu.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.448
That's pretty good.
That's pretty flavorful.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.484
There are some other main-course
options from UK Ikeas

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.252
which unfortunately we
couldn't find today.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.721
These include such things
as butternut squash

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:19.125
and sweet potato soup;
Mangalore chicken curry;

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:22.595
butternut squash, blue cheese,
and caramelized onion pie;

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:26.132
chili sin carne; garlic
butter chicken pie;

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:27.500
and leek and potato soup.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.101
I would like to move on to the sides.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.437
Right here we have the

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:34.407
vegetable medallions.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.708
I like veggies presented like this,

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.044
just like in a little
puck. Just bite into it.

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.946
Looks like it has some broccoli,

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:43.249
mostly potato friendly, little onion.

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:45.117
Yeah, not bad. Decent side.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:48.955
It's like broccoli potatoes,
like broccoli mashed potatoes.

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:51.357
That Havana chicken that
I mentioned earlier,

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:53.392
this is the beans and rice it comes with.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.261
I don't know if they mix them
up or it just got mixed up

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:58.364
in transit, but, you know,
beans and rice. Let's go.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.833
This is just white rice and black beans.

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:04.503
I don't taste any additional
flavor to this at all.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.572
They do sometimes offer plantains.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:09.742
Again, the Ikea we went to
today did not have plantains,

00:10:09.742 --> 00:10:11.911
but they did have a garlic bread.

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:16.582
I think that's an exclusive.

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.884
On to the Ikea cold dishes.

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:22.088
They have a veggie dog.

00:10:22.088 --> 00:10:25.291
Well, the veggie dog wrap
is under the cold dishes

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:27.660
according to the script,
and this veggie dog is cold.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.561
Maybe it's been sitting a while.

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:30.129
Either way, it's not very good.

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:33.633
Also, they have a Greek
salad, also the Caesar salad,

00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:36.002
which, once again, I mean,
this is pretty low effort.

00:10:36.002 --> 00:10:39.338
A Stockholm salad,

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:41.674
not to be confused with
Stockholm syndrome,

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:43.809
which I'm starting to feel
right now eating this food.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:46.812
Salmon, lettuce, lemon.

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:50.016
Sure.

00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:51.584
That's not bad, actually.

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:56.222
I like this sauce that's
turning color under these lights

00:10:56.222 --> 00:10:57.823
and this salmon.

00:10:57.823 --> 00:11:00.459
We're not quite sure
what is in this salad,

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:04.397
what the sauce is right now,
but due the miracle of editing,

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:06.966
we can put that on the screen right,

00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:08.334
and that's what it is.

00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:09.502
Tastes pretty good.

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:13.806
Also, you can get a BLT chicken wrap.

00:11:13.806 --> 00:11:16.942
Not bad if you like wraps
and BLT and chicken.

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.445
Also at a US Ikea, which was not available

00:11:19.445 --> 00:11:22.248
at time of filming this
at our Burbank Ikea,

00:11:22.248 --> 00:11:26.185
is a Greek veggie ball
wrap and marinated salmon.

00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:28.854
The UK's cold-plate menu is
pretty bland in comparison.

00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:31.590
The only one they had today was
this marinated salmon plate,

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.593
but we can also get an egg
and shrimp sandwich with mayo,

00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:37.329
marinated salmon wrap, small salad bowl,

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:39.098
and a tomato and mozzarella salad.

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:40.866
I guess I'll give the salmon a quick try.

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:42.601
I do like smoked salmon.

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:44.236
Here, of course, they call it gravlax

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.238
because it's the traditional Swedish way,

00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:48.808
and it comes with a dill
sauce and some lemon.

00:11:48.808 --> 00:11:49.642
Fairly mild flavor.

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:52.011
I like the kind of herb
crusting that you get.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:54.647
The dill sauce is pretty dilly.

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:55.981
And now on to desserts.

00:11:55.981 --> 00:11:58.918
There are three exclusive
Ikea US desserts.

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:00.319
I was only able to get one of them.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:02.221
So, the first would be
the strawberry shortcake,

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:03.956
not available at time of shooting this.

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:06.258
The second is this, the
caramel almond cake.

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:10.596
And the third is the infamous
chocolate layered cake,

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:12.698
also known as the conspiracy cake.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.067
I asked everyone there,

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.670
"Please tell me you have chocolate cake."

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.271
And they all said no.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:23.442
No chocolate cake at the
Burbank Ikea, today, at least.

00:12:23.442 --> 00:12:25.044
Tragically, we don't
have the conspiracy cake

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:26.612
here in the UK, but we do have some other

00:12:26.612 --> 00:12:27.980
exclusive dessert options.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:31.050
For example, this
delightful-looking strawberry tart.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.918
There's some real pieces
of strawberry in there.

00:12:32.918 --> 00:12:34.620
I like the pastry, I like the cream,

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.788
I like the fresh strawberries.

00:12:35.788 --> 00:12:39.325
Whatever the kind of
strawberry syrup jelly stuff

00:12:39.325 --> 00:12:41.694
that they've put around
the outside is, it's OK,

00:12:41.694 --> 00:12:44.830
but it has a slightly, almost
medicinal quality to it

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.367
that I don't really love. It
almost reminds me of Calpol.

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:49.468
I don't know if you have that in the US,

00:12:49.468 --> 00:12:50.870
but it's a medicine

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.105
that's marketed towards
children in the UK.

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:56.008
Next up, we have Ikea's famous Daim cake.

00:12:56.008 --> 00:12:58.043
Now, you do have this on
the menu in the US, however,

00:12:58.043 --> 00:12:59.779
I believe you guys call it
something slightly different.

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:01.213
I think caramel almond cake.

00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:03.349
Is Daim not a particularly
big brand name in the US?

00:13:03.349 --> 00:13:05.551
Because over here in the
UK I'd say most people

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:08.587
are familiar with Daim
as a chocolate brand.

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:11.323
Harry was just talking a
minute ago about the Daim cake,

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.559
the diam cake, D-I-A-M cake?

00:13:13.559 --> 00:13:15.561
I've never heard of it. I've
never heard of that brand.

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:18.430
I have no idea what it is, I'm
sorry, but we do have this,

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.432
which I think is supposed to be similar.

00:13:23.435 --> 00:13:25.971
Oh, yeah. This is fantastic.

00:13:25.971 --> 00:13:26.906
I'm getting one of these every time I go.

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:28.240
I'm going to get one of these,
and I'm going to get that

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.075
chocolate cake. I'm going to
be on the lookout for it now.

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:32.678
It's maybe not quite as popular
in the UK as it used to be.

00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:33.846
It reminds me of my grandad a lot

00:13:33.846 --> 00:13:35.347
because he used to really love a Daim bar.

00:13:35.347 --> 00:13:37.750
I wouldn't see many people
my age going for it,

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.019
but still very tasty if
you're in the mood for it.

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:42.354
And this cake is sensational.

00:13:42.354 --> 00:13:45.124
You get these layers of chocolate,

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:47.760
this kind of biscuity crumb,
and these kind of, like,

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:50.196
almost pancakes in the middle.

00:13:50.196 --> 00:13:52.398
I think these dividing
lines might almost be

00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:55.234
kind of cold, chilled pancakes.

00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:57.303
This might be my favorite
thing on the menu.

00:13:57.303 --> 00:13:59.672
This is why I'm making
excuses to go to Ikea.

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:02.508
Mm.

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:05.177
They did have these at the register,

00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:08.380
and this also says Daim
on it. Have we seen that?

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.083
Yeah. OK, this tastes like this.

00:14:11.083 --> 00:14:12.484
Never heard of this, but it's very good,

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:13.652
and this is fantastic.

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.721
Maybe they just rebranded
it because no one in the US

00:14:15.721 --> 00:14:18.490
knows what ... Daim cake? Diam cake is?

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.392
Our next dessert option is a cheesecake

00:14:20.392 --> 00:14:21.994
with blueberries and raspberries.

00:14:21.994 --> 00:14:24.530
It's a very soft cheesecake,
really easy to cut.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.333
There's a nice baked crumb on top.

00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:28.567
There's a layer of the berry stuff,

00:14:28.567 --> 00:14:30.569
so there's some blueberries
in there, some raspberries.

00:14:30.569 --> 00:14:31.403
Then finally we have these

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:33.706
Under the Sea rocky road biscuits.

00:14:33.706 --> 00:14:35.875
Obviously, rocky road
in the UK is a dessert,

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:37.843
which is usually a no-bake
dessert made of things

00:14:37.843 --> 00:14:41.013
like melted chocolate,
golden syrup, marshmallows,

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:43.382
even things like cornflakes,
pieces of biscuit,

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:45.384
that sort of thing, all
just kind of mixed together,

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:47.553
left to set, and then you
have a nice easy dessert.

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:49.188
It turns out what makes this Under the Sea

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:51.323
is that they have a kind of animal stamp

00:14:51.323 --> 00:14:54.393
in icing on top of it. Here
we have this nice octopus,

00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:56.428
and here we have a couple of dolphins.

00:14:58.464 --> 00:15:00.099
I think when I eat a rocky road

00:15:00.099 --> 00:15:02.868
I kind of want some
more distinct elements.

00:15:02.868 --> 00:15:05.237
I like being able to bite
into it and crunch through

00:15:05.237 --> 00:15:07.773
a bit of biscuit or chew
through a raisin or something.

00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:10.142
Whereas with this one, it's
kind of all blended together,

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:12.111
so you don't really get
the texture contrasts.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:13.913
The flavor's very much there.
It's still all those elements

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:15.281
that I'm used to in terms of the flavor.

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:17.216
You may also be able to find
some other dessert options

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:19.184
on a UK menu which we couldn't find today.

00:15:19.184 --> 00:15:21.854
These include things like a
caramelized biscuit cheesecake,

00:15:21.854 --> 00:15:25.658
a chocolate clementine bomb,
an elderflower and lemon cake,

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:28.527
a gooey chocolatey cake,
a lemon cheesecake,

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:30.863
rhubarb and custard cake,
and a strawberry jelly.

00:15:30.863 --> 00:15:32.865
Aside from its restaurant, Ikea also has

00:15:32.865 --> 00:15:35.167
the Swedish bistro for quick bites.

00:15:35.167 --> 00:15:38.370
The bistro serves quick bites
like hot dogs and pizza slices

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.773
that you can generally grab
on your way out of the store.

00:15:40.773 --> 00:15:43.776
A few exclusives we had,
of course, was pizza slice.

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:45.244
There it is.

00:15:45.244 --> 00:15:46.612
I went with cheese.

00:15:46.612 --> 00:15:50.449
Is this like Costco where, like, surprise,

00:15:50.449 --> 00:15:51.984
Ikea has amazing pizza?

00:15:53.619 --> 00:15:55.254
This is a really good slice of pizza.

00:15:55.254 --> 00:15:58.023
I can't tell, but I think
this was oven-cooked,

00:15:58.023 --> 00:15:59.992
fire-oven-cooked, not
just like the pizza oven.

00:15:59.992 --> 00:16:03.095
This has, like, a,
yeah, like a brick oven.

00:16:04.263 --> 00:16:06.832
It's not as good as Costco,
but it's pretty good.

00:16:06.832 --> 00:16:09.768
Wow, weird. Ikea's got good
pizza. Good on you, Ikea.

00:16:09.768 --> 00:16:13.339
You can also get this
giant bistro pretzel.

00:16:13.339 --> 00:16:15.674
Look at this little,
like, a little braid here.

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:16.709
Look at me, I'm a Jedi.

00:16:16.709 --> 00:16:18.844
But you are not a Jedi yet.

00:16:18.844 --> 00:16:20.045
And it comes with mustard.

00:16:20.045 --> 00:16:21.580
They didn't have the mustard either, man.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.949
I don't know, is it because I
went at 10:30 in the morning

00:16:23.949 --> 00:16:25.985
and the stuff hadn't shown up yet?

00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.286
They didn't have anything.

00:16:29.755 --> 00:16:31.357
A pretzel with no mustard.

00:16:33.025 --> 00:16:34.660
No, no.

00:16:36.662 --> 00:16:38.130
You need to dip in something.

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.665
Also at the US Ikea bistro,

00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:42.234
you can get a marinated salmon baguette.

00:16:42.234 --> 00:16:43.068
They didn't have it.

00:16:43.068 --> 00:16:45.738
We have a few exclusive bistro
options of our own in the UK.

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:48.140
Firstly, if you like the
onions on the hot dog,

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.376
you can just get a side of fried onions.

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:53.746
Next up we have these,
which are chick'less strips.

00:16:53.746 --> 00:16:57.282
So, these are a plant-based
version of a chicken tender.

00:16:57.282 --> 00:16:58.350
I'd say they look pretty good.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.185
They kind of passed the visual test.

00:17:00.185 --> 00:17:02.121
Yeah, when I tore this apart I was worried

00:17:02.121 --> 00:17:03.722
that the texture wasn't going to be right,

00:17:03.722 --> 00:17:04.990
and unfortunately it's not.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.558
It's very spongy, it's very mushy.

00:17:06.558 --> 00:17:07.726
It just needs a little bit more texture.

00:17:07.726 --> 00:17:08.961
Just something to make it resemble

00:17:08.961 --> 00:17:10.496
a chicken tender a little bit more.

00:17:10.496 --> 00:17:12.398
Obviously when you get an
actual piece of chicken tender

00:17:12.398 --> 00:17:13.966
or chicken breast, you
can kind of tear it,

00:17:13.966 --> 00:17:15.801
and you see those strips and the fibers.

00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:17.069
They just really haven't got that here.

00:17:17.069 --> 00:17:17.970
Flavor's not too bad, though.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.205
We can also get chips
from the bistro in the UK.

00:17:20.205 --> 00:17:22.141
It doesn't seem like you
guys can do this in the US.

00:17:22.141 --> 00:17:24.243
We have our veggie dog option,
which comes with the same

00:17:24.243 --> 00:17:25.878
toppings as the regular hot dog.

00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:26.912
So, here we've got fried onions.

00:17:26.912 --> 00:17:28.380
You can also get some with pickles.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:31.483
The veggie dog in the UK isn't
a plant-based-meat thing,

00:17:31.483 --> 00:17:32.951
it is just vegetables.

00:17:32.951 --> 00:17:35.988
So it looks like there's some
kale in there, some carrot,

00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:37.423
maybe, like, some mustard seeds.

00:17:37.423 --> 00:17:39.191
I think that, with the fried onions,

00:17:39.191 --> 00:17:40.659
with the pickles and some sauce,

00:17:40.659 --> 00:17:42.394
actually a pretty good veggie option.

00:17:42.394 --> 00:17:45.097
Then we have some drink
options, notably milkshakes.

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:47.433
In the UK you can get
milkshakes in four flavors,

00:17:47.433 --> 00:17:49.501
vanilla, chocolate,
strawberry, and banana.

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:51.870
We got a banana one
today. Have a little sip.

00:17:53.806 --> 00:17:56.041
That's not bad. Pretty
gentle banana flavor.

00:17:56.041 --> 00:17:57.843
It's mostly just ice cream
but with a little bit

00:17:57.843 --> 00:18:01.080
of flavoring in that,
which, who could say no?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.215
Ikea in the UK does serve
breakfast, although unfortunately

00:18:03.215 --> 00:18:05.217
when we arrived today
they weren't serving it.

00:18:05.217 --> 00:18:06.685
The options that you'll
find there are pretty much

00:18:06.685 --> 00:18:07.786
everything that you would normally find

00:18:07.786 --> 00:18:10.289
on a full English breakfast,
so it includes things like

00:18:10.289 --> 00:18:12.524
bacon, sausages, hash browns,

00:18:12.524 --> 00:18:15.994
beans, tomatoes, mushrooms, black pudding.

00:18:15.994 --> 00:18:18.464
Sometimes you'll find things
like tattie scones as well,

00:18:18.464 --> 00:18:20.566
and you can also get
white or wholemeal toast.

00:18:20.566 --> 00:18:21.733
If breakfast platters aren't your thing,

00:18:21.733 --> 00:18:24.303
then you can also just go for
some fruit or some porridge.

00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:25.971
Breakfast!

00:18:25.971 --> 00:18:29.241
The breakfast platter in the
US also comes in both regular

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:32.911
and small sizes and is made
up of eggs, potatoes, bacon,

00:18:32.911 --> 00:18:35.280
Swedish pancakes, and now
it's supposed to be topped

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.449
with the lingonberry jam, and
they didn't give it to us!

00:18:37.449 --> 00:18:39.852
The US breakfast menu also offers

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:43.288
a skagen croissant sandwich,
which is a croissant

00:18:43.288 --> 00:18:46.959
filled with traditional
Swedish shrimp salad.

00:18:46.959 --> 00:18:48.026
They didn't have it.

00:18:48.026 --> 00:18:51.263
I think Ikea has its own
line of drinks available

00:18:51.263 --> 00:18:54.099
in its restaurants. The US
Ikeas, you'll find cola,

00:18:54.099 --> 00:18:57.002
sugar-free cola,
sparkling raspberry juice,

00:18:57.002 --> 00:18:59.705
lingonberry juice, and sparkling lemonade.

00:18:59.705 --> 00:19:02.407
I went ahead and got
the lingonberry juice.

00:19:03.275 --> 00:19:04.610
Straight up, no idea
what a lingonberry is,

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:05.911
but it's fantastic.

00:19:05.911 --> 00:19:07.513
There's no difference in the size cups.

00:19:07.513 --> 00:19:09.414
You just have glasses
that are the same size

00:19:09.414 --> 00:19:11.250
or these to-go cups or whatever.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.885
We have some drink options
at the restaurant in the UK

00:19:12.885 --> 00:19:14.520
that you guys might not have in the US.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.988
There are a couple of options for kids,

00:19:15.988 --> 00:19:18.223
which are these Pip Organic juices.

00:19:18.223 --> 00:19:20.359
We have a couple of
Robinsons options in the UK.

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:22.628
Robinsons is probably the
most popular brand of squash

00:19:22.628 --> 00:19:24.429
in the UK, and this is basically just

00:19:24.429 --> 00:19:26.265
a diluted version of their squash.

00:19:26.265 --> 00:19:28.667
Squash, for those who don't
know, is a concentrated,

00:19:28.667 --> 00:19:30.869
fruity drink that you kind of water down

00:19:30.869 --> 00:19:32.538
to have a nice refreshing beverage.

00:19:32.538 --> 00:19:34.273
You can get a peach and mango version

00:19:34.273 --> 00:19:36.074
or a raspberry and apple version.

00:19:36.074 --> 00:19:37.376
And if you feel like celebrating

00:19:37.376 --> 00:19:38.810
any of your purchases
that you've just made

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.313
from the Ikea, you can also get alcohol.

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:44.917
We have three alcoholic options
on the menu at a UK Ikea,

00:19:44.917 --> 00:19:49.121
a rosé wine, a red wine, or a dark lager.

00:19:49.121 --> 00:19:51.423
Finally, Ikea has a Swedish
market where you can buy

00:19:51.423 --> 00:19:53.625
prepackaged food items to take home.

00:19:53.625 --> 00:19:55.527
The items on offer include
some of their classic foods,

00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:57.663
like the meatballs,
which you can buy frozen,

00:19:57.663 --> 00:19:59.831
or some gravy sachets,
which you can make at home.

00:19:59.831 --> 00:20:01.667
In the UK, you can also
find the plant-based balls

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:02.701
on offer in there.

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:04.436
You can get a whole frozen Daim cake,

00:20:04.436 --> 00:20:06.572
which I'll be taking home
and eating all by myself.

00:20:06.572 --> 00:20:08.273
And speaking of Daim, you
can also get the chocolate

00:20:08.273 --> 00:20:09.575
which the cake is based on.

00:20:09.575 --> 00:20:11.677
Here it's in bite-sized form rather than

00:20:11.677 --> 00:20:13.879
as actual chocolate
bars, but as you can see,

00:20:13.879 --> 00:20:16.348
it's chocolate with a kind
of hard caramel center.

00:20:16.348 --> 00:20:17.416
Charlie has dibs on these.

00:20:17.416 --> 00:20:21.787
Another thing at the US Ikea,

00:20:22.721 --> 00:20:24.556
maybe not exclusives per se,

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:28.827
but of course they have a
whole thing of frozen stuff.

00:20:28.827 --> 00:20:30.362
I just grabbed stuff that was interesting.

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:33.131
Come on, the Cinnabons, huh?

00:20:33.131 --> 00:20:34.499
The cinnamon buns.

00:20:34.499 --> 00:20:35.534
Meatballs.

00:20:35.534 --> 00:20:39.037
And, you know we were talking about

00:20:39.037 --> 00:20:40.772
the Daim cake,

00:20:40.772 --> 00:20:45.711
but they do have, it's
frozen to take home,

00:20:45.711 --> 00:20:47.713
and of course it is the Daim cake.

00:20:50.549 --> 00:20:52.484
Let's compare the nutritional
information of some iconic

00:20:52.484 --> 00:20:54.553
Ikea dishes in the US and the UK.

00:20:54.553 --> 00:20:57.456
In the UK, eight Ikea meatballs
contains the following:

00:20:57.456 --> 00:20:59.224
342 calories,

00:20:59.224 --> 00:21:01.226
25.1 grams of fat,

00:21:01.226 --> 00:21:02.694
8.2 grams of carbs,

00:21:02.694 --> 00:21:05.530
and 856 milligrams of sodium.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.100
In the US, the same plate
of Swedish meatballs contain

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:09.501
304 calories,

00:21:09.501 --> 00:21:11.570
22.4 grams of fat,

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.639
6.4 grams of carbs,

00:21:13.639 --> 00:21:16.441
592 milligrams of sodium.

00:21:16.441 --> 00:21:19.111
The UK takes this round in every category.

00:21:19.111 --> 00:21:20.379
What about the Ikea hot dog?

00:21:20.379 --> 00:21:24.216
In the US it contains 260
calories, 15 grams of fat,

00:21:24.216 --> 00:21:28.186
24 grams of carbs, and
780 milligrams of sodium.

00:21:28.186 --> 00:21:31.957
And in the UK, the hot
dog contains 293 calories,

00:21:31.957 --> 00:21:35.627
15.2 grams of fat, 29.5 grams of carbs,

00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:37.629
and 708 milligrams of sodium.

00:21:37.629 --> 00:21:39.931
Looks like the UK version
is higher in calories

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:42.334
and fat once again. USA, baby.

00:21:45.103 --> 00:21:47.372
What's actually in the
iconic Ikea meatballs?

00:21:47.372 --> 00:21:49.107
According to the Ikea
website, if you want to make

00:21:49.107 --> 00:21:51.843
their meatballs at home, use
the following ingredients:

00:21:51.843 --> 00:21:56.315
beef mince, pork mince, onion,
garlic, bread crumbs, milk,

00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:58.583
egg, and salt and pepper to taste.

00:21:58.583 --> 00:22:00.085
But is that actually the ingredients list

00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:01.486
for proper Ikea meatballs?

00:22:01.486 --> 00:22:04.323
Well, on the back of the frozen packet,

00:22:04.323 --> 00:22:05.691
you'll find an ingredients list.

00:22:05.691 --> 00:22:09.861
According to this packet, they
contain beef, pork, water,

00:22:09.861 --> 00:22:13.098
bread crumbs, egg, dried onion,

00:22:13.098 --> 00:22:15.467
salt, egg powder,

00:22:15.467 --> 00:22:17.803
black pepper extract, and allspice.

00:22:17.803 --> 00:22:19.438
Overall, it seems like it's
pretty close to the list

00:22:19.438 --> 00:22:21.406
that they gave you on the
website, with a few more things

00:22:21.406 --> 00:22:23.675
like powdered ingredients
versus fresh ingredients,

00:22:23.675 --> 00:22:25.210
and a couple of spice differences too.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:29.181
I wasn't able to find it online

00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:31.216
or in the cafeteria,

00:22:31.216 --> 00:22:33.452
the ingredients list, but I got here

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:38.657
the frozen precooked meatballs,

00:22:38.657 --> 00:22:39.958
and those ingredients ...

00:22:39.958 --> 00:22:41.493
hm, actually not bad.

00:22:41.493 --> 00:22:43.595
Assuming these are the ones
that they have in the cafeteria

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:47.366
in the US, the ingredients
for this is beef, pork,

00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:50.102
water, bread crumbs made
of unbleached wheat flour,

00:22:50.102 --> 00:22:51.303
salt, and yeast,

00:22:51.303 --> 00:22:55.006
whole eggs, salt,
dehydrated onion, egg white,

00:22:55.006 --> 00:22:57.876
that's not plural. Egg white, singular.

00:22:57.876 --> 00:22:59.177
Spices.

00:23:00.512 --> 00:23:03.382
That's not bad, I think, for
a prepackaged product, right?

00:23:03.382 --> 00:23:05.817
It's like, well, that's, you
know, what's in them, right?

00:23:05.817 --> 00:23:07.586
While we're on the subject
of Ikea ingredients,

00:23:07.586 --> 00:23:09.054
one thing that UK viewers might remember

00:23:09.054 --> 00:23:11.156
was our infamous horsemeat scandal.

00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:15.560
Back in 2013, a number of foods

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:17.929
in the UK claiming to be beef or pork

00:23:17.929 --> 00:23:20.665
were actually found to
contain traces of horsemeat.

00:23:20.665 --> 00:23:22.667
While this wasn't
necessarily a health issue,

00:23:22.667 --> 00:23:24.636
it did raise some major
questions concerning

00:23:24.636 --> 00:23:27.105
the traceability of foods
throughout supply chains,

00:23:27.105 --> 00:23:29.875
and unfortunately Ikea was
also caught up in this scandal.

00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:31.877
Czech authorities found
traces of horsemeat

00:23:31.877 --> 00:23:34.246
in some Ikea meatballs that
had been produced in Sweden

00:23:34.246 --> 00:23:35.680
and shipped all around Europe.

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.416
Thankfully, the horsemeat
meatballs were found

00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:38.784
before they reached consumers.

00:23:38.784 --> 00:23:42.254
In total, 760 kilograms of
meatballs were destroyed.

00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:43.755
Given the fact that
there's no health concerns

00:23:43.755 --> 00:23:45.323
related to the consumption of horsemeat,

00:23:45.323 --> 00:23:46.491
I think they should have
just leaned into it.

00:23:46.491 --> 00:23:47.359
Just passed them off as, like,

00:23:47.359 --> 00:23:49.227
limited-edition horse meatballs,

00:23:49.227 --> 00:23:51.029
and just go with it, lads, it's fine.

00:23:53.598 --> 00:23:56.234
Ikea's food is almost suspiciously cheap,

00:23:56.234 --> 00:23:58.003
and it's actually one of
the ways it tricks you into

00:23:58.003 --> 00:24:00.572
spending more time and
money in its stores.

00:24:00.572 --> 00:24:03.308
Ikea is basically willing
to take its losses

00:24:03.308 --> 00:24:04.776
with its cheap food prices

00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:07.612
because it's counting on you
to spend a bunch of money

00:24:07.612 --> 00:24:09.748
on furniture and other household items.

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:13.018
A former Ikea executive even
referred to the meatballs

00:24:13.018 --> 00:24:15.020
as the "best sofa seller."

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:17.989
In the UK, a plate of
eight meatballs, peas,

00:24:17.989 --> 00:24:20.725
mash or chips, gravy, and lingonberry jam

00:24:20.725 --> 00:24:22.727
will set you back just £4.95.

00:24:22.727 --> 00:24:25.697
At the time of recording,
that's around $6.49.

00:24:25.697 --> 00:24:26.998
I do have to say, that's really cheap.

00:24:26.998 --> 00:24:28.333
I don't think the quality's that bad.

00:24:28.333 --> 00:24:30.802
It's really tasty food and,
yeah, it's a real bargain.

00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:33.071
I will make an effort
to go via the restaurant

00:24:33.071 --> 00:24:34.272
if I'm just going through Ikea.

00:24:34.272 --> 00:24:36.341
Even if I'm just popping in
for, like, one or two bits,

00:24:36.341 --> 00:24:38.109
I'm going to sit down,
eat a plate of meatballs.

00:24:38.109 --> 00:24:39.978
It's good value, it's tasty, I love it.

00:24:39.978 --> 00:24:43.281
An eight-meatball meal in the US is $9.99,

00:24:43.281 --> 00:24:45.417
which in the UK is £7.80.

00:24:45.417 --> 00:24:48.887
That's a 54% increase in the States.

00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:53.859
Overall I would say Ikea is
pretty popular in the UK.

00:24:53.859 --> 00:24:56.428
It's most people's go-to
for basic furniture

00:24:56.595 --> 00:24:57.796
and household needs, I would say,

00:24:57.796 --> 00:24:59.831
especially when people are buying a house

00:24:59.831 --> 00:25:01.666
or moving house or something like that.

00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:04.503
Personally, I love Ikea.
I love going there.

00:25:04.503 --> 00:25:07.706
I do enjoy a trip. It's
fun. I like the food.

00:25:07.706 --> 00:25:09.407
I like walking around
and pretending, like,

00:25:09.407 --> 00:25:10.775
"Ooh, that could be my apartment

00:25:10.775 --> 00:25:12.177
or my bedroom or my kitchen."

00:25:12.177 --> 00:25:13.778
I wouldn't say Ikea is
somewhere I go often,

00:25:13.778 --> 00:25:15.914
particularly because I live
in quite central London,

00:25:15.914 --> 00:25:17.315
and there aren't many in Central London.

00:25:17.315 --> 00:25:18.917
I think they're trying to
open one on Oxford Street

00:25:18.917 --> 00:25:21.386
right now. At the time of
recording this, it wasn't open,

00:25:21.386 --> 00:25:22.854
but they're kind of trying to get there.

00:25:22.854 --> 00:25:24.856
But so, like I say, it's more
of a place where you'll go

00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:27.058
specifically when you
need to do an Ikea shop.

00:25:27.058 --> 00:25:29.394
Ikea is so popular here.

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:31.796
I think it's popular in the whole country.

00:25:31.796 --> 00:25:34.366
The one in Burbank, we went
there at 10:30 in the morning.

00:25:34.366 --> 00:25:38.670
It opens at 10, and at 10:30,
parking lot was pretty full.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:40.272
The cafeteria line was full.

00:25:40.272 --> 00:25:42.374
So I'd say Ikea's pretty popular.

00:25:42.374 --> 00:25:44.609
I personally wouldn't go
to Ikea just for the food.

00:25:44.609 --> 00:25:46.745
Again, it might be because
I don't live close enough

00:25:46.745 --> 00:25:48.280
to one to make that worthwhile.

00:25:48.280 --> 00:25:50.015
I do love the food. The
meatballs are great.

00:25:50.015 --> 00:25:51.683
Like I say, the desserts are fantastic.

00:25:51.683 --> 00:25:53.752
But I don't like it to
the extent that I would

00:25:53.752 --> 00:25:56.488
make the effort to travel
to one just to eat there.

00:25:56.488 --> 00:25:59.124
I'm not going to say I
go to Ikea for the food,

00:25:59.124 --> 00:26:03.361
but the food definitely is a
good motivator to go to Ikea.

00:26:03.528 --> 00:26:05.363
I will say overall I
do enjoy the experience

00:26:05.363 --> 00:26:06.731
of going to an Ikea.

00:26:06.731 --> 00:26:08.466
I am aware that it's kind of designed

00:26:08.466 --> 00:26:09.534
to make us spend money.

00:26:09.568 --> 00:26:11.503
Obviously the restaurant
plays a part of this as well,

00:26:11.503 --> 00:26:13.171
because it's kind of
encouraging you to make a day

00:26:13.171 --> 00:26:15.373
of your trip to Ikea, really
spend some time there,

00:26:15.373 --> 00:26:17.475
sit down, take a break in
the middle of the day, eat,

00:26:17.475 --> 00:26:19.511
re-energize yourself for more shopping.

00:26:19.511 --> 00:26:21.046
And as you can guess by
my friends on the table

00:26:21.046 --> 00:26:23.248
with me here, I do think that
their marketing is a really

00:26:23.248 --> 00:26:25.417
clever ploy to make us spend
more money there as well.

00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:28.053
I'm joined here by my friend Djungelskog.

00:26:28.086 --> 00:26:30.622
I'm really sorry, I'm going to
butcher these pronunciations.

00:26:30.622 --> 00:26:34.359
And my friend Blåhaj, who
is the adorable little shark

00:26:34.359 --> 00:26:37.095
who is also, I think, a
trans icon. Love that.

00:26:37.095 --> 00:26:38.096
You'll often see things like this

00:26:38.096 --> 00:26:40.265
really getting a
reputation on the internet,

00:26:40.265 --> 00:26:42.467
driving more commerce to Ikea stores.

00:26:42.467 --> 00:26:44.135
I don't know if they're
doing that deliberately

00:26:44.135 --> 00:26:47.105
or if it's just kind of a
side effect of making some

00:26:47.105 --> 00:26:48.573
very, very cute plush toys.

00:26:48.573 --> 00:26:50.508
But everyone, I think, will generally have

00:26:50.508 --> 00:26:52.010
at least one thing from
Ikea in their home.

00:26:52.010 --> 00:26:54.346
So whatever they're doing,
it's kind of working.

00:26:54.346 --> 00:26:55.547
I'm not mad about it either.

00:26:55.547 --> 00:26:57.983
I support Ikea. Keep
up the good work, guys.

